		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=23850#p23850"><![CDATA[
Software Developer<br><br>Location: Singapore<br><br>Join the cutting edge of 3D software! Autodesk's tools bring 3D to life in blockbuster films and games with products that include Autodesk Maya and Autodesk 3ds Max.<br><br>We are looking for a software developer for Autodesk Softimage, a character modeling and 3D animation product from Autodesk's Media and Entertainment (M&amp;E) division. In this position, your primary role will be the design and development of features and workflows aimed at professionals who use Softimage.<br><br>We are looking for someone with solid software engineering experience and passionate about 3D computer graphics, with the ability and desire to tackle problems in multiple domains such as usability, new algorithms, feature enhancement, data exchange and performance tuning. <br><br>This role is located at the Autodesk Singapore Research and Development centre (ASRD). ASRD is one of the largest product development facilities among multinational companies in Singapore, expanding the Autodesk global engineering and software development program. Activities here include the development of components and technologies for a range of products from all of Autodesk's product divisions.<br><br>Responsibilities:<br><br>As a generalist, this role will help develop new workflow features and maintain existing ones in various modules of Softimage.<br><br>Requirements:<br>"5 years C++ on Windows<br>Experience with simulation (e.g. particle, face and muscle simulation) and related math and physics required."<br><br>If interested, please send your updated profile with CTC details and Notice Period.<br><br>Regards<br>Manish<br>99866 12009<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=8283">thegreatm</a> — Tue Jun 14, 2011 10:28 am</p><hr />
